### Additional Information

The only current in-tree caller is the accompanying spec test, which does not assert on the return value, so the bug has gone unnoticed. However, any future use of `removeFunction` to wrap a deprecated API that has a meaningful return value (for instance, a getter-style function being removed in a breaking change) would silently receive `undefined` from the wrapper and break downstream callers during the deprecation window.

I will open a PR that forwards the return value (mirroring `renameFunction` / `moveAPI`) and extends the existing spec to assert that both the return value and the `this` context of the deprecated function are preserved.
